Contract change rule
====================

The contract is tools.json (tool names, parameters, result shapes, error
messages the suite matches on), journal.md (event kinds and the journal
schema) and runtime.md (process start).

Any change to a tool name, a parameter (name, type, optionality, allowed
values), a result shape, or a journal event shape bumps `tool_schema` by one
in tools.json, in the same commit, and adds an entry below. A change to
`journal_schema` (the `v` field) also bumps `tool_schema`. Wording changes
that alter no schema and no matched error text do not bump it.

The plugin declares the `tool_schema` it requires; both implementations and
the conformance suite read the value from tools.json. contract/check_contract.py
fails on a tool_schema value other than the one it expects, a tool-list change,
an example that violates its schema, a missing state_matrix cell or an errors row
without a valid precedence number.

Log (newest first)

(no bump, 2026-11-21, issue #109)  the configured skill-name list (REQ-24) gains
query-walkthrough in both builds, and the UserPromptExpansion hook matcher becomes
`^(grill-me|query-walkthrough)$`; no tool name, parameter, result shape or journal event
shape changes, so tool_schema stays 4.

(no bump, 2026-11-21, issue #102)  runtime.md "Signals and shutdown limits": states that
a stdin EOF shutdown completes pending replies before exit 0 and that a signal shutdown
may cut a reply the client has not read (both builds); removes the claim that a stalled
stdout reader blocks the TypeScript handler (three clauses); the "Once only" bullet now
says that in TypeScript a signal during the EOF drain ends the wait with status 0; a stalled
EOF drain ends after 5 s with status 0 (reply tail dropped, journal flushed; Rust has no
ceiling there); no request is processed after a shutdown starts. No
tool, parameter, result shape or journal event changes.

(no bump, 2026-11-21, issue #96)  runtime.md: the working names are final (set A).
Process names `regspike-rs`, `regspike-ts` and `regspike.mjs` become `register-rs`,
`register-ts` and `register.mjs`; environment variables `REGSPIKE_IMPL`,
`REGSPIKE_TS_BUNDLE` and the test-only `REGSPIKE_CLOCK_OFFSET_SECONDS` become
`REGISTER_IMPL`, `REGISTER_TS_BUNDLE` and `REGISTER_CLOCK_OFFSET_SECONDS` (the env
table in runtime.md and its pin in contract/check_contract.py change together). The
serverInfo names become `register-rs` and `register-ts` (the suite requires a name
and version, not these values). No tool, parameter, result shape or journal event
changes.

(no bump, 2026-11-21, user decision, issue #90)  runtime.md, journal.md and
docs/requirements.md (REQ-27 rule 5 and the active row) extend the 2026-11-16
stdin-EOF decision to SIGINT, SIGTERM and SIGHUP: each runs the same shutdown as
stdin EOF (queue flush, decision log, pid file removal) and exits with 128 plus
the signal number (129, 130, 143; EOF stays 0). New runtime.md section "Signals
and shutdown limits": the ends table names the four triggers, the always-handle
policy for signals the parent ignored at spawn (and the unmeasured `nohup claude`
caveat), the Rust 5 s bound on an in-flight request (expiry equals SIGKILL), the
absence of a bound in TypeScript and its start-up window of about 40 ms.
Behaviour change in both builds (new scenarios S-27f to S-27n) and a wording
change in the contract; no tool name, parameter, result shape, journal event
shape or error text changes, so tool_schema stays 4 and journal_schema stays 2.
Why: Claude Code stops the server with SIGINT, so a normal session end wrote no
decision log and left a stale pid file (docs/evidence/live-run-4.md). SIGKILL and
crashes are unchanged.

(no bump, 2026-11-19, user decision Q9)  tools.json errors table: the first
resume|discard row's "when" reads "no id given and nothing unfinished"
(was "no unfinished journal exists"). Behaviour is unchanged and both builds
already agree: an id that names no unfinished journal gives "unknown interview
id: <id>" even when no journal exists at all. The "when" text is not served in
tools/list (name, description and inputSchema only) and no scenario matches it;
the matched message text is unchanged, so tool_schema stays 4.

(no bump, 2026-11-18, user decision Q3)  tools.json records the rule both
builds already implement and S-32b asserts: a volunteered `source: user`
answer in log_item needs a user prompt counted since the previous check_stop
call. New errors row (precedence 10, before the volunteered-answer cap), a
clause in the log_item description and in error_precedence row 10. The
suite matches the rejection on "prompt" only and no shape changes, so
tool_schema stays 4.

(no bump, 2026-11-18)  contract/tools.json: end_interview input gains a top-level
"type": "object" next to its oneOf. Claude Code 2.1.327 rejects a tools/list whose
inputSchema lacks it, which hid every model-facing tool in a live run. The accepted
inputs are unchanged (the oneOf branches were already objects), so tool_schema stays 4.

(no bump, 2026-11-17)  contract/classifier.md, label and inline-code details decided
by the user: a line-start list marker must be followed by a space or tab (`-Q1.` is
not a label); numbered markers take any number of digits (`10. Q1.`); a closing
`*`/backtick wrapper is allowed after the label on line-start forms (`**Q1**.`);
only single-backtick inline code is stripped before the `?` test (a `?` in a
double-backtick span counts); the `reason` of an unlogged block stays unspecified.
Wording only, so tool_schema stays 4.

(no bump, 2026-11-17)  contract/classifier.md: the finish-attempt classifier rules
(label forms, stripping, finish attempt, concerned items, content words, the
88-word stop list, empty-message rule) and the note that `unknown` is covered by
implementation unit tests only. Restates build plan 5.1 and adds the decisions of
2026-11-17; no tool name, parameter, result shape or journal event shape changes,
so tool_schema stays 4.
------------------

tool_schema 4  (decision round of 2026-11-17)
Entries are appended as the decisions land; all belong to this one bump.
- Version bump only in this commit: tools.json, runtime.md heading and
  statement, check_contract.py, the selftest and every scenario's
  begin_interview now carry tool_schema 4. journal_schema stays 2.
- resolve rule: the model-source rejection applies to a parent that has children
  but fewer than N (REQ-35), not to a parent with zero children, which is an
  ordinary item (user decision 2026-11-17). Wording fix in the resolve error
  row and the kind-rules summary; the behaviour was already so in S-35c.
- check_stop overflow wording pinned (REQ-45): after the first 10 open items the
  reason says `N more` (N = open items not listed); nothing when 10 or fewer.
  S-45c already pinned it.
- Finish gate: a parent resolved by the user (source user) is exempt from the
  under-size flag, as a user-parked parent already was (REQ-35). A parent
  resolved by the model and left with children but fewer than N stays flagged.
- note_prompt ignores harness-injected agent-message prompts (user decision
  2026-11-17). A prompt whose text begins, at character 0 with no trimming, with
  the exact characters `<agent-message ` (V10 form `<agent-message from="<id>">`)
  is a complete no-op returning {}: no prompt count, prompt_seen, budget or
  user-prompt-since refresh, hook_health count, last_seen_session_id update or
  journal event. Behaviour change, no new field or event, so journal_schema
  stays 2.
- Budget wording (user decision 2026-11-17): the per-prompt budget governs and
  there is no ordering rule between a prompt and model actions or Stop calls
  (REQ-32 amended). "Budget point" is defined (conventions.budget_point): one
  unit of the per-prompt allowance max(1, p), flat 4 when the classifier returned
  unknown. Error rows reworded to use it; messages and behaviour unchanged.
- Six confirmed hook behaviours written down (conventions.hook_rules): block
  caps count blocks only; the per-prompt cap of 2 is shared by finish and
  unlogged blocks; a fail-open allow leaves the interview active and writes the
  log; stop events only while active; quoted lines stripped before the ?
  test; hook_health.note_prompt is 1 after a start preceded by inactive prompts.
  Text only, no schema change.
- Hook output contract (REQ-41, V8 verified 2026-11-17): hook-facing tools return
  only empty text or the exact documented JSON shape (note_prompt, skill_started:
  empty or {}; check_stop: {} or the decision object), because the harness acts
  on any returned text that parses as JSON with decision or hookSpecificOutput
  keys.

tool_schema 3  (review fixes after the three independent reviews, 2026-11-16)
Entries are appended as the fixes land; all belong to this one bump.
- begin_interview: in state pending it engages the interview (returns state
  active, existing true); `existing` is now required and `state` is narrowed to
  active|complete. Why: the old text made the hook-start plus begin_interview
  route leave the interview pending and stood down (review S1-1).
- Error channel: domain failures must be isError:true tool results, never
  JSON-RPC errors (the old text let the suite accept either, which weakened
  REQ-40/REQ-71 identical behaviour).
- Journal flush: the queue is also flushed on stdin EOF (user decision), not
  only at check_stop and at end. Why: a graceful exit must lose no event.
- State enums: status.state is none|pending|active|complete (an ended
  interview reports none, REQ-27 "none: entered ... after ended"); resume.state
  is the const active; the end_interview result end_kind no longer lists
  `abandoned`, which is journal-only (session change). Why: unreachable and
  ambiguous values let two implementations diverge (review S2-5).
- State x tool matrix (tools.json state_matrix) and numbered error precedence
  (error_precedence): every cell of the REQ-27 table now has a stated result or
  error; a failing call changes nothing (never starts, engages or revives an
  interview). Why: two implementations diverged on unspecified cells (S1-2).
- end_interview: `abandon` is now the const true, `abandon` and `reason`
  require each other, and `mode: plain` excludes both (a oneOf); four new error
  rows (nothing to end, pending without mode plain, mode plain outside pending,
  abandon with nothing open). Why: these cells were unspecified (review S1-2).
- resolve|park|reopen on an unknown id: error row `no such item: <id>`; such a
  call never starts or engages an interview (review S1-2).
- resume and discard: error rows for no unfinished journal, unknown id, a
  live-owned journal (distinct from "journal already claimed"), several
  journals without an id, wrong state; discard is accepted in none and pending.
  Why: only the claim/several/state/replay rows existed (review S1-2).
- Error rows added: invalid arguments (any tool), subquestion without parent,
  decision-item answer by the model through log_item (REQ-34), per-prompt budget
  spent and volunteered-answer cap (REQ-32); every row now carries `check`, its
  number in error_precedence. Why: required rejections had no row (S2-8).
- Single-line patterns: the rationale pattern (new $defs.oneline) and the id
  pattern reject a trailing newline and the line separators VT, FF, NEL, U+2028,
  U+2029; a trailing `$` means end of string and the Python checker translates
  it to \Z. Why: Python's `$` matched "ok\n" while ECMAScript/Rust did not, so
  suite and servers disagreed (review S3-1).
- Item/tree schema: $defs.item is a oneOf by status (Open all-null; Stale keeps
  its answer/source/rationale; Parked needs parked_by and park_reason; Resolved
  needs non-null answer, source and single-line rationale). `stale` removed from
  the log_item, resolve and park results (only reopen can make items Stale,
  REQ-36). Tree order pinned: Open, Stale, Parked, Resolved, creation order
  within a group. Why: REQ-31 states must be unrepresentable (review S2-7).
- status.resumable is an array (empty when none) of {interview_id, last_event},
  most recently modified journal first. Why: REQ-52 allows several unfinished
  journals; a single object hid the others (review S2-6). version_mismatch
  lifetime pinned (set by a mismatch, cleared by a later match).
- Decision log pinned in runtime.md (directory rule, file name, modes,
  journal_position header line, mode and end_kind strings); status gains a
  required decision_log (path or null) and the end_interview result a required
  decision_log path. Why: the log was not in the contract, so REQ-63 replay
  could not find or compare it (review S2-1).
- Id generation pinned: interview id iv-<UTC timestamp>-<8 hex>, item id Q<n>
  (next unused). Why: counters (iv-1) would collide across server restarts and
  archive rename-onto-existing would break (review S2-2). Examples updated.
- Pid file pinned: one-line JSON {pid, start, interview_id}, start time from
  /proc/<pid>/stat field 22, exact-equality liveness, the stale-replace
  (rename aside, verify, O_EXCL create) sequence and orphan pruning. Why: REQ-52
  gave pid and start time but no format, and O_EXCL cannot replace a crashed
  owner's file (review S2-3, build-plan F1).
- Pending interview fates: replaced-by-resume, server exit while pending and
  session change each write an `end` event (stood_down, mode not_engaged) and
  archive the journal, so no ghost unfinished journal remains; mode `plain` is
  reserved for end_interview mode plain; "Interview ends and server exit" table
  in runtime.md. Why: a hook start journals a pending interview, and nothing
  ended it on those paths (review S2-4).
- Journal details: hook vs prompt vs stop (one `hook` event per hook call,
  `prompt`/`stop` additional), hook_health derivation, `stop.blocks` is an
  object {prompt, finish, unlogged}, `resume.from_seq` equals the result
  `last_event` (pre-resume), `start.route/implicit/skill/session_id` rules,
  `mismatch` rule, replay failure modes (torn final line ignored; invalid JSON,
  gap, unknown kind fail naming the line), v1 shape. Why: counters and caps
  must replay identically (review S2-9, S2-10, S3-4).
- `_meta` test pinned: presence of the key claudecode/toolUseId (a _meta
  without it is hook-style); check_stop always returns JSON text, never empty
  text. Why: runtime.md and tools.json disagreed (review S2-11, S3-2).
- status gains a required write_error (string or null); unwritable data
  directory behaviour pinned (fail open, in-memory continues, retry). Why:
  REQ-50 fail-open was unspecified for storage failure (review S3-8).

(no bump, 2026-11-17, walk Q1)  tools.json descriptions of begin_interview and
skill_started state that the exact-match skill-name list (REQ-24) applies to the
hook route (skill_started) only, and that begin_interview accepts any non-blank
skill name. This restates existing behaviour (the none-state row already says an
unlisted name is accepted); no shape, parameter or error text changes, so
tool_schema stays 3.

(no bump, 2026-11-16, conformance review S2-7)  contract/journal.schema.json is
the machine-readable form of journal.md's envelope and 13 event kinds (JSON
Schema subset, with good and bad examples); check_contract.py ties it to the
journal.md event table, and the conformance runner validates every journal line
against it. It restates the existing journal shape and changes none, so
tool_schema stays 3 and journal_schema stays 2.

(no bump, 2026-11-16)  runtime.md "Journal location": exact path template,
project-key derivation (SHA-256 of CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR), archive folder, modes
0700/0600 and the temp-directory fallback. Run-time layout only; no tool name,
parameter, result shape or journal event shape changes, so tool_schema stays 2.

tool_schema 2  (slice C1 walkthrough, 2026-11-16)  Journal format change, and a
result-shape narrowing: `interrupted` removed from the journal `end` event's
end_kind enum and from the `end_interview` result enum (a crash or server exit
on an active interview writes no `end` event; `interrupted` is a decision-log
kind only). End-kind triggers stated in journal.md. Added without schema change:
`log_item` duplicate caller-supplied id error row, and the rule that `status`
`items` counts equal the counts derived from `tree` (checked in check_contract.py).
Bumped because the CHANGES rule counts a journal event shape change.

tool_schema 1  (slice C1, 2026-11-16)  Initial freeze: REQ-40 tool list,
journal_schema 2.
